        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "229300ad-8425-57ec-89bd-d9559704d4cb",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Bank Street, Central, Hong Kong\n- Buildings: HSBC Main Building, Bank of China Building\n- Companies: The Hongkong and Shanghai Banking Corporation, HSBC Holdings, Bank of China (Hong Kong)\n- Roads: Des Voeux Road Central, Queen's Road Central\n\nFacts:\n- Bank Street is a short street in Central, Hong Kong.\n- Bank Street links Des Voeux Road Central to Queen's Road Central.\n- Bank Street is named for its location between the HSBC Building and the Bank of China Building.\n- The HSBC Building and the Bank of China Building were the former headquarters of The Hongkong and Shanghai Banking Corporation and Bank of China (Hong Kong), respectively.\n- HSBC Main Building is a headquarters building of The Hongkong and Shanghai Banking Corporation.\n- The Hongkong and Shanghai Banking Corporation is now a wholly owned subsidiary of London-based HSBC Holdings.",
